[Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  every four years with the Olympics  municipalities compete to host the  winter and summer games and virtually  always plunge their cities and sometimes  even their home countries into massive  debt and insolvency why because host  cities inevitably spend double or more  of our initial estimates fewer people  show up than expected in the  International Olympic Committee or IOC  takes bigger and bigger cuts of TV and  other revenue streams sports economist  Andrew Zimbalist says that a typical  Summer Olympics generates up to six  billion dollars in revenue at least half  of which goes to the IOC  Winter Games generate even less money  despite often being more expensive to  host than Summer Games cities routinely  claim that whatever money they spend on  new facilities will stimulate the local  economy for decades to come with the  recent announcement that Paris will host  the 2024 Summer Games and Los Angeles  will host the 2028 Summer Games  here are five cities that got [ __ ] by  hosting the Olympics Athens is the  birthplace of the ancient games that  inspired today's modern municipal money  pets its 2004 games cost sixteen billion  dollars or ten times the original  estimate by 2010 more than half the  venue's built for the event were  underused completely empty or literally  falling apart at 50 billion dollars the  Sochi Winter Games cost more than all  previous Winter Olympics combined paid  for by a dwindling supply of Russian  petrodollars and gold bullion Boris  Nemtsov documented that 21 billion  dollars went for embezzlement and  kickbacks for businessman Friends of  Vladimir Putin Nemtsov was later  assassinated  [Music]  played by low ticket sales partly due to  the outbreak of the Zika virus the Brio  games ended up costing twenty billion  dollars rather than the thirteen billion  dollars backers claimed and the  showplace Maracana stadium which got a  five hundred million dollar makeover was  largely abandoned soon after 